    description: "Per INV-tuzub-sufuk-... (concept-tag shape uniformity, violated) and audit report /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept_tag_audit_04172026_0335.md:\n\nmiddleware_chain.py:81-82 filters concepts with a list[str] membership test ('middleware' not in concepts) while framework_patterns.py emits list[dict]. The filter is therefore always True for the continue branch in production, making the linker silently inert (zero middleware-chain edges emitted on real repos, despite tests passing).\n\nFix (mirrors subprocess_cli.py::_has_command_concept pattern):\n\n  - Change middleware_chain.py:81-82 from\n      concepts = sym.meta.get('concepts', [])\n      if 'middleware' not in concepts: continue\n    to\n      concepts = sym.meta.get('concepts', [])\n      if not any(isinstance(c, dict) and c.get('concept') == 'middleware' for c in concepts): continue\n\n  - Update tests/test_middleware_chain_linker.py _sym helper (lines 25-31) and all fixtures (line 171 etc.) to use the production emitter shape: concepts=[{'concept': 'middleware'}] instead of ['middleware'].\n\n  - Add an integration smoke test that uses framework_patterns.py's actual emitter path (a symbol matched against express/fastapi middleware YAML pattern) and verifies the linker emits the expected chain edges.\n\nAcceptance: (1) linker tests still pass with new fixture shape, (2) integration test demonstrates the linker works against the real emitter, (3) bakeoff on a repo that uses express middleware shows non-zero middleware_chain edges."  # 53f5
    fields: {}  # 53f5
